      "children": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Angus Comyns is a Canberra-based Screen Print and Stencil Artist whose work spans canvas, walls, and everything in between — bold, layered, and instantly recognisable. He needed a personal brand that could hold its own against the intensity of the art itself."
            }
          ],
          "type": "p",
          "id": "L47qItz1NZ"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "id": "xiZqSBkRD_",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "In collaboration with "
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Pat Rose"
                }
              ],
              "type": "a",
              "url": "https://rickrose.com.au/",
              "id": "yt_gAkak48"
            },
            {
              "text": " under the Oddjobs banner, I led a full-spectrum brand and content engagement covering every touchpoint of his creative identity. The project encompassed logo design and complete brand identity development, a custom website and integrated online store, and a professional photography suite capturing both portraiture and detailed documentation of his finished works."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "id": "ib3j9q3iPs",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Beyond the static, we embedded ourselves in his process — producing on-location video content that followed Angus as he developed new pieces. This culminated in a series of short-form documentary edits designed to give audiences genuine insight into his creative method and vision."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "id": "gfQ0nkXKWB",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The deliverables extended into print and interactive publishing, with two bespoke catalogues produced: one for traditional print distribution and a second optimised for touchscreen presentation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
